    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a2">

                <pb facs="0433" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg353"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Zaldo to Mr.
                            Squiers</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-06-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: The President, to whom I have
                    communicated your attentive note, No. 8, of the 14th instant, instructs me to
                    say to your excellency that it would be <pb facs="0434" n="354" xml:id="pg354"/>
                    exceedingly pleasant to him to accede to your request with regard to the Chinese
                    immigrants who may have undertaken the voyage before the promulgation of the
                    immigration law of the 15th of May of this year, but the text of the law being
                    so definite it is not possible for him to give any such instructions as your
                    excellency indicates, as in doing so it would be tantamount to an infraction of
                    the said law.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos de Zaldo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
